= Related Work

Specifically related to the realistic aspect of the work, several studies have been conducted: between them, a 2022 study, "The use of virtual reality in environment experiences and the importance of realism" tested, in the second study, how realism can impact people that are recovering from a stressful situation reacted to several levels of realism in virtual reality environment@study.

The paper describes how presence obtained higher scores on high realism environments and immersion was partially compromised by the virtual space size@study.

However, the study put an emphasis on scenes with not a high level of interaction, while our game, while providing a less realistic scene, involves more interaction and involvement in the virtual world, therefore allowing to understand how a higher level of interaction could compromise the lower level of realism, allowing a higher sense of presence and immersion.

Other papers that analyzed how to intensify horror experiences exist, like the 2023 "Decoding Fear: Exploring User Experiences in Virtual Reality Horror Games"@study2, also exists.